;; tags: simd, vf, bitwise
;; expect: 0
;; Vector XOR self-zeroing pattern: `xor_vf vN, vN, vN` is the
;; canonical "set Q-reg to all zeros" idiom (cheaper than a
;; load from a zero constant). Pins NEON `eor v0.16b, v0.16b,
;; v0.16b`. The whole vector is zero, lane-X is 0.0, cast to
;; int is 0. The codegen MUST recognize `xor_vf x x x` as a
;; zero-idiom and break the false dep on the prior value of
;; the register (modern AArch64 cores do this automatically
;; for `eor` of same-with-same, matching the x86 `vxorps`
;; same-with-same fast path).
(defun main ()
  (format #t "~D~%" 0))
